+## Changed
+
+- Added `crates/kernel/config/src/blocks/gates.rs` with the `Gates` struct
+  (`commit_retries: u64`), its `DEFAULT_COMMIT_RETRIES = 2` default and
+  `read_gates`, which checks `gates` keys before reading `commitRetries`.
+- Added `value::non_negative_integer`, beside `positive_integer`, which allows
+  0, reports `WrongType` with `an integer`, and reports a negative value as
+  `InvalidValue` with `must be a non-negative integer`.
+- Added `Config.gates`, read from the `gates` table after `limits`, and the
+  `gates` top-level key; `Config::default()` uses `Gates::default()`.
+- Exported `Gates` from the crate root and documented it with
+  `Implements: rust-config/gate-settings`; tagged `Config` with
+  `Implements: rust-config/config-file`.
+- Added `crates/kernel/config/tests/config_gates.rs` proving every row of the
+  "Gate values" table, tagged `Covers: rust-config/gate-values`.
+- Updated `unknown_top_level_key` in `tests/config_file.rs` to the `[server]`
+  text and the `server` key.
+- Ran `cargo fmt --all`; `cargo test -p osq-kernel-config --test config_gates
+  --test config_file` passes, `OSQ_CHANGE=... sh scripts/verify-rust.sh`
+  passes, and a manual `cargo mutants` run over `gates.rs`, `value.rs` and
+  `config.rs` caught all 29 mutants.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- Added `Implements: rust-config/config-file` to the `Config` struct doc even
+  though the task only requires public items added by this task to carry a
+  tag, so the changed public type ends its doc with one too.
+
+Touched: crates/kernel/config/src/blocks/gates.rs, crates/kernel/config/src/blocks/mod.rs, crates/kernel/config/src/blocks/value.rs, crates/kernel/config/src/config.rs, crates/kernel/config/src/lib.rs, crates/kernel/config/tests/config_gates.rs, crates/kernel/config/tests/config_file.rs
